{"schema": 1, "kind": "review", "id": "rev-20261125T001059Z-16ffec03", "ts": "2026-11-25T00:14:10Z", "actor": {"worktree": "prawduct", "plugin": "3.9.1-dev", "branch": "feature/test-determinism", "build": "276ed9b5e02a+dirty"}, "body": {"base_commit": "276ed9b5e02a4be97699d0fbdf46d3f227188fa5", "base_tree": "b24519c7303d8b1dc80c0e95b355999f881dc21c", "head_tree": "daa9dacc6216fd71b37ec02bfad39589b750f71b", "head_commit": null, "dispatch_commit": "276ed9b5e02a4be97699d0fbdf46d3f227188fa5", "mode": "verify-resolutions (delta review, prior findings only)", "mode_chosen_by": "explicit-args", "stage": "inner", "tier": "escalate", "roster": [{"role": "reviewer", "model": "claude-opus-5-5"}], "files_reviewed": ["plugin/bin/prawduct-hook", "plugin/docs/discipline.md", "plugin/docs/test-determinism.md", "plugin/docs/waivers.md", "plugin/lib/determinism_lint.py", "plugin/lib/record_lint.py", "plugin/methodology/building.md", "plugin/skills/critic/goals-1-3.md", "plugin/skills/critic/review-protocol.md", "plugin/skills/janitor/SKILL.md", "plugin/skills/janitor/themes.md", "plugin/templates/test-specifications.md", "tests/test_critic_consolidate.py", "tests/test_determinism_lint.py", "tests/test_discipline_table.py", "tests/test_hook_argument_shape.py", "tests/test_record_lint.py", "tests/test_reviewer_payload_budget.py", "tests/test_v5_methodology.py"], "files_changed": [".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-test-determinism.md", ".prawduct/owner-rulings.md", "plugin/bin/prawduct-hook", "plugin/docs/test-determinism.md", "plugin/lib/determinism_lint.py", "plugin/skills/critic/goals-1-3.md", "plugin/skills/critic/review-protocol.md", "tests/test_determinism_lint.py"], "files_oracle": [".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-test-determinism.md", ".prawduct/owner-rulings.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/api-contract.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/architecture.md", ".prawduct/changes/test-determinism.md", ".prawduct/cross-cutting-concerns.md"], "findings": [], "counts": {"blocking": 0, "warning": 0, "note": 0}, "observations": [{"goal": "Nothing Is Unintended", "title": "R-1's construction excludes suffixless files and a few code-capable data suffixes", "recommendation": "The construction is right: no allowlist remains, and `_subject` reports every non-Python file under a test tree whose suffix is not in `_DATA_SUFFIXES`. Two edges still pass silently. A file with no suffix, such as an executable `tests/run` shell suite, returns '' because the check requires `suffix and ...`. `.sql` (pgTAP), `.html` (QUnit pages) and `.xml` can also hold test code and are in the data set. Both are narrow, so no edit is wanted unless a product meets them. If one is ever made, count a suffixless file under a test tree as `other`.", "about": {"review_id": "rev-20261124T234435Z-e6b3faf9", "fid": "R-1"}, "oid": "O-1"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "title": "R-2: text keys fix attribution except for textually identical reads, and the import check's insert-above is not pinned", "recommendation": "Keying clock sites by the stripped line text lands an insert-above finding on the new line (`test_a_new_read_above_an_old_one_is_reported_at_its_own_line`). Two gaps remain. First, when the new read's text is identical to an old one's in the same function or module, the Counter surplus goes to whichever site `ast.walk` yields last, and waiving the old line still lets the new one pass. Second, the pinned case covers `test-clock-fake` only, not `test-clock-import`, although both share the key shape. A side effect, not a defect: editing a line that holds an existing read, including a formatter's rewrap, now reports that read as introduced. Narrow, so no edit is owed.", "about": {"review_id": "rev-20261124T234435Z-e6b3faf9", "fid": "R-2"}, "oid": "O-2"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Unintended", "title": "R-3's placement change is stated in test-determinism.md but not in waivers.md's test-scope row", "recommendation": "Record gap, so it rides the commit this uncommitted delta still owes. `_waived` now accepts only the site's line or a comment-only line above it, and `docs/test-determinism.md` \u00a7 Waiving a site says so. `plugin/docs/waivers.md`'s `test-scope` row still ends 'Matched on the line or the one above.' A builder who follows that row and puts a trailing waiver on the previous statement gets a finding the row says cannot happen. That fails closed, so nothing is broken, but the row is wrong. Make it relational (say this row is matched on its own line or a comment line above) in the same commit.", "about": {"review_id": "rev-20261124T234435Z-e6b3faf9", "fid": "R-3"}, "oid": "O-3"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Unintended", "title": "R-5: is_test_path now uses pytest's directories, but three Python-path predicates still use every ecosystem's", "recommendation": "`is_test_path` now classifies `.py` files by `_PY_TEST_DIRS` alone. `_project_roots`, `_first_party` and `_package_of_init` still exclude Python paths by `_TEST_DIRS`, which adds `spec`, `specs`, `__tests__` and `*.test`/`*.tests` directories. For example, a product subpackage `myapp/specs/__init__.py` that imports all its submodules is never a P2b candidate. These are false negatives only, so this is noted and no edit is owed. If touched, use `_PY_TEST_DIRS` wherever the path is Python.", "about": {"review_id": "rev-20261124T234435Z-e6b3faf9", "fid": "R-5"}, "oid": "O-4"}], "duration_seconds": 660, "scope": "test-determinism", "scope_chosen_by": "binding", "scope_unresolved_cause": null, "scope_reason": null, "base_extended_from": null, "chunks": ["03"], "chunks_proposed": ["03"], "chunks_declared": false, "chunks_evidence": {"03": {"paths": [], "paths_more": 0, "commits": ["276ed9b5e02a"]}}, "base_reviewed": null, "record_lint": {"records": [".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-test-determinism.md", ".prawduct/owner-rulings.md", "plugin/docs/test-determinism.md", "plugin/skills/critic/goals-1-3.md", "plugin/skills/critic/review-protocol.md"], "chunk_graded": "03", "chunks_graded": ["03"], "plan_graded": ".prawduc